-- title:
--   Surjection from the blow-up chart onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic frame.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asks for a ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(T)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(T)\!)$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(T)\!)$, of the $q$-expansion function field of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times$, namely the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$).
--
--   **The base ring and the $j$-chart.** Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A\to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\subseteq L\subseteq K$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero, mapping in $L(\!(T)\!)$ to the image of the $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under `coeffEmb L`. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy, by `hϖt`, $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A K j` for $j$ regarded as an element of $C$.
--
--   **A supersingular closed point.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, and let `hss` require: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no non-trivial point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The integral model and the point $z$.** Let $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin`, `fInf` from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and $\varpi_z$ the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism for $A$ followed by global sections of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258); the hypothesis `hz` puts $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$. Let $y'$ be a point of `XFin A K j` $=\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin A K j` sending $y'$ to $z$, satisfying the same supersingularity condition `hss'` for its prime ideal, and let `hy'y` assert $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$.
--
--   **The local model at $z$.** Let $W_1$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, let $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ be a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, and let $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1-$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=f_1-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)$ in $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto
--   $$S:=W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v_1-f_1u_1\big),$$
--   and write $\mathrm{mk}_S$ for the quotient map. Throughout, `germY` denotes the ring homomorphism $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ given by the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism for $C$, followed by the inverse of the canonical isomorphism `appIso` of `ιFin A K j` on the top open set, followed by the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin A K j`; and $\Psi:=e_1\circ(\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}):C\to S$, where $\mathrm{toC}$ is the canonical map from the stalk to its completion. Put $\mathfrak M:=\big(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi),\,\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1\big)$ and $\mathfrak M_t:=\big(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\,\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1\big)$, ideals of $S$.
--
--   **The blow-up chart.** Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ and let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which, by `hB`, is the restriction of scalars of the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x\in K:\exists\,i\in J,\ x\,\varpi_t=i\}$, i.e. $B=C[\,i/\varpi_t:i\in J\,]$; the hypothesis `hCB` records $C\subseteq B$.
--
--   **Hypothesis `hbridge`** (nine clauses): $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak M)=y$; for every $n$ and every $s\in S$ there is $a\in C$ with $\Psi a-s\in\mathfrak M^{\,n}$; $\Psi(a)=\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1 a)$ for every $a\in A$; every $c\in C$ is congruent modulo $y$ to the image of an element of $A$; every $w\in W_1$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ to $\sigma_1a$ for some $a\in A$; $\sigma_1^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{W_1})=\mathfrak m_A$; $\mathfrak M$ is maximal; every maximal ideal of $S$ equals $\mathfrak M$; and $S$ is flat as a $C$-module through $\Psi$.
--
--   **Hypothesis `hcentre`** (four clauses): the ideal of $S$ generated by $\Psi(J)$ is $\mathfrak M_t$; there is an ideal $I$ of $C$ with $J=\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak M_t)\cap I$ and $I+y=C$; $J\subseteq y$; and the image of $\varpi_t$ in $C$ lies in $J$.
--
--   Finally, the residue field $\kappa_A:=$ `ResidueField A` is given as an algebra over `GaloisField q 2`, the field with $q^2$ elements.
--
--   **Conclusion.** With the above notation, let $L_{\mathrm{loc}}:=$ `Localization.Away (mkS (MvPowerSeries.C (σ₁ ϖt)))`, let $\iota_S:S\to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ be the localisation map, set
--   $$x_0:=\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_SX_0)\cdot\big(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)\big)^{-1},\qquad x_1:=\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_SX_1)\cdot\big(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)\big)^{-1},$$
--   the inverses being `IsLocalization.Away.invSelf`, and let $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ be the subring of $L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ generated by $\iota_S(S)\cup\{x_0,x_1\}$. Write $D:=$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), the quotient of $\kappa_A[X_0,X_1]$ by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q (ResidueField A)` $-1$, with [`DrinfeldCurve.x q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L42) and [`DrinfeldCurve.y q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L44) the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   Then for every ring homomorphism $\Phi:B\to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, every proof that $\iota_S(S)\subseteq R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, that $x_0,x_1\in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ and that $\Phi(B)\subseteq R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, every ring homomorphism $t_W:W_1\to\kappa_A$, every $c_R\in\kappa_A$ and every ring homomorphism $\rho_R:R_{\mathrm{loc}}\to D$ subject to:
--
--   (a) $\Phi$ restricted to $C$ equals $\iota_S\circ\Psi$;
--
--   (b) for all $x\in B$ and $i\in J$ with $x\,\varpi_t=i$ in $K$, one has $\Phi(x)\cdot\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))=\iota_S(\Psi i)$;
--
--   (c) $t_W(\sigma_1a)=\mathrm{res}_A(a)$ for all $a\in A$, and $t_W$ vanishes on $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$;
--
--   (d) $c_R\neq 0$;
--
--   (e) $\rho_R(\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_SF))$ is the image in $D$ of $t_W(\mathrm{constantCoeff}\,F)$ for every $F\in W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$;
--
--   (f) $\rho_R(x_0)=c_R\cdot$ [`DrinfeldCurve.x q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L42) and $\rho_R(x_1)=c_R\cdot$ [`DrinfeldCurve.y q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L44), the scalars being taken through $\kappa_A\to D$;
--
--   (g) $\rho_R$ is surjective;
--
--   (h) for $r\in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$, $\rho_R(r)=0$ if and only if $r$ lies in the ideal of $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ generated by $\iota_S(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi))$;
--
--   there exists a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to D$ such that: $\rho(b)=\rho_R(\Phi b)$ for all $b\in B$; $\rho$ is surjective; for $b\in B$, $\rho(b)=0$ if and only if $b$ lies in the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ under the inclusion $C\subseteq B$; and $\rho(a)=$ the image in $D$ of $\mathrm{res}_A(a)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   This is the local computation of the special fibre of the blow-up chart $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$ at a supersingular point: it transports a surjection of the localised formal model $R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring over the residue field of $A$ down to a surjection $B\to\kappa_A[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ with kernel $yB$ and compatible with the residue map of $A$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_blowupChart_ringHom_localBlowupChart_surjective_ker_eq_span_of_dense_of_flat).
